# "Draw a card, then discard a card" (CR 608.2c): the draw comes first, so a hand that is empty when Refute resolves draws
# one card and then discards that very card - it ends empty, and the drawn Island is in the graveyard. In the other order
# the discard would find nothing and the hand would end with the drawn card. Bot1 empties its hand on turn 1 by casting six
# zero-cost artifacts, then pays {1}{U}{U} with two Mox Sapphires and a Mox Jet to counter Bot2's Llanowar Elves.

[Bot1 Deck]
Refute
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Ornithopter
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 1
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Refute.Cast(Target: Stack.Llanowar Elves)
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Island)

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Refute; Island
Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves
Stack.Count = 0
